From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: dts: ingenic: thingino-t31: add ISP node and MSC1 pinmux

The generic thingino-t31 leaf has no `isp` label and no MSC1 pin group.
Fragments that open either label are skipped by inject-camera-dtsi.sh, and
no T31 board can start tx-isp without the ISP node.

Add:
 - an enabled `isp` node; every T31 board running the mainline kernel
   needs tx-isp, and the open driver maps 0x13300000 itself (it does not
   bind through DT);
 - an `msc1_pb` group using the new "mmc1" pins, so a board can enable
   MSC1 SDIO.

--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/thingino-t31.dts
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/thingino-t31.dts
@@ -19,6 +19,12 @@
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0x0 0x8000000>;
 	};
+
+	isp: isp@13300000 {
+		compatible = "ingenic,t31-isp";
+		reg = <0x13300000 0x100000>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
 };
 
 &exclk {
@@ -167,4 +173,11 @@
 		function = "i2c1";
 		groups = "i2c1-data-b";
 	};
+
+	/* SDIO WLAN pins (PB8-11/PB13-14), matching the board's use of MSC1
+	   for the SDIO WiFi rather than the MAC. */
+	msc1_pb: msc1-4bit {
+		function = "mmc1";
+		groups = "mmc1-1bit", "mmc1-4bit";
+	};
 };
